    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Kansas City and Omaha Railroad reached Holstein in 1887, prompting the village to be platted that same year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.adamshistory.org/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=24:holstein&catid=5"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Holstein incorporated in June 1889, covering a six‑mile‑long by three‑mile‑wide area that made up half of Cottonwood Township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.adamshistory.org/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=24:holstein&catid=5"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1908, a brick schoolhouse replaced the two‑story frame building, which was moved south of the tracks on Depot Street and used as an opera house for years.",
